## Attributes on blocks

{.lead}
A leading paragraph can carry a class and be styled differently without
HTML escape hatches in the prose.

## Code with language hints

```python
from myst_parser.parsers.docutils_ import Parser
from docutils.core import publish_parts

html = publish_parts(source=text, parser=Parser(), writer_name="html5")["html_body"]
```

## Strikethrough and smart punctuation

~~Markdown is enough~~ — until it isn't. "Curly quotes", em-dashes — and
ellipses... all come through without extensions fighting each other.
